Fix context menu action buttons not opening the edit drawer

The "Add New Row" and "Edit row/cell" buttons in the floating action menu
were dismissing the menu but not opening the drawer.

Root cause: the document-level `mousedown` handler that dismissed the menu
on outside clicks was racing with the button's `onClick`. When the user
pressed down on an action button, the mousedown event fired first and called
`setContextMenu(null)`. By the time the React `onClick` fired `openDrawer()`,
the `contextMenu` guard check (`if (!contextMenu) return`) exited early,
so the drawer never opened.

Fix: replaced the `stopPropagation` approach with the correct click-outside
pattern — a `ref` on the menu container that lets the dismiss handler skip
events originating inside the menu:

  if (contextMenuRef.current?.contains(e.target as Node)) return;

This guarantees clicks on action buttons are never treated as outside clicks,
so `contextMenu` is always truthy when `openDrawer` reads it.
